er statistic, and advances only at or beyond the leader startIndex. Leader commit notification records commitment/configuration and queues the committed prefix to the FSM. Commands complete after single/batch application; barriers pass through the same worker; no-ops can finish without an FSM callback. Error checks differ between ordinary transport and pipeline future consumption, retained as a local contract lead rather than an assumed valid report.',['B-dispatch','B-append','B-replicate','B-pipeline','B-pipeline-producer','B-snapshot-send','B-install','B-commit','B-consume','B-fsm'],['F-local','F-reply','F-match','F-pipeline-match','F-snapshot-match','F-commit'],['S-api','S-admit','S-dispatch','S-append','S-replicate','S-pipeline','S-pipeline-contract','S-net-pipeline','S-snapshot-send','S-snapshot-install','S-commit','S-consume','S-prepare','S-fsm-rest']),context=p('Startup reads stable term/log tail, installs snapshot metadata and normally restores FSM, then scans later configuration entries before workers start. Bootstrap seeds clean state; forced RecoverCluster and Restore explicitly permit disaster-recovery replacement. Follower contact timeout and latest voter eligibility enter candidacy. Optional pre-vote tests proposed authority without persisting term, then real election persists term/self-vote and counts voter-targeted replies on campaign-local channels. Receivers enforce term, known-leader, candidate eligibility, prior-vote and history-order checks. Higher-term requests/replies, inadequate recent voter contact, negative verification or committed self-removal can cause authority loss. Transfer waits for target replication progress then TimeoutNow starts a normal majority election with transfer exceptions. Independent heartbeats refresh contact and verification separately from durable log support.',['B-startup','B-bootstrap-recover','B-follow-timeout','B-prevote','B-election','B-vote','B-persist','B-heartbeat','B-lease','B-transfer','B-verify','B-config-change'],[],['S-startup','S-startup-restore','S-bootstrap','S-recover','S-follow','S-prevote-send','S-prevote-recv','S-election','S-vote','S-persist','S-heartbeat','S-lease','S-transfer','S-timeout-now','S-verify-start','S-verify-consume','S-config-append']),connection=p('Each leadership generation creates zeroed voter matches and startIndex=lastIndex+1, dispatches a no-op, and gives workers the generation commitment pointer and step-down channel. Exit stops workers and fails remaining inflight/verification futures; already committed FSM tuples survive on their serialized queue. Durable prior logs constrain new elections by term/index freshness, but need fresh generation support before commitment. Configuration changes require the prior configuration and a current-term entry committed; latest configuration immediately changes voter filtering, preserving matches by continuing ID. Snapshot creation binds an applied FSM boundary to a committed configuration before log compaction, while startup/installation restores those contexts. User Restore aborts remaining inflight work, serializes restoration after queued FSM work and burns a log index so subsequent replication uses the snapshot; its special recovery contract is distinct from normal preservation.',['B-generation','B-config-change','B-snapshot-create','B-startup','B-install','B-user-restore','B-fsm','B-persist','B-vote'],['F-commit','F-installed'],['S-leader','S-peers','S-config-append','S-config-scan','S-snapshot-create','S-startup','S-startup-restore','S-snapshot-install','S-restore-user','S-restore-contract','S-fsm-rest','S-persist','S-vote']),open_details=['Pipeline future Error/Response discipline is a sourced local lead; consensus consequences not assumed.','VerifyLeader callback eligibility differs from voter-filtered commitment and needs contract comparison.','Stable-store partial failure/crash semantics, concrete snapshot/log backend variants and legacy compatibility schedules remain open.','Failed follower